---
source: crates/sluice-cli/tests/help.rs
expression: "help(&[\"--help\"])"
---
Usage: sluice [OPTIONS] <COMMAND>

Commands:
  id           Print the endpoint id of this machine's identity, or replace the identity
  completions  Print the completion script for a shell
  send         Send files and folders, print a ticket, and serve until one complete download
  recv         Receive what a ticket names, writing it under the current folder by default
  doctor       Check the home, who can reach it, its lock and identity key, and say how to fix a problem
  help         Print this message or the help of the given subcommand(s)

Options:
      --json
          Print JSON, one object per line, instead of text. A failure is then a JSON line on stderr

      --color <WHEN>
          When to colour help, errors and other output. NO_COLOR set to anything turns it off

          Possible values:
          - auto:   Colour a stream only when it is a terminal
          - always: Colour always, unless `NO_COLOR` is set
          - never:  Never colour
          
          [default: auto]

  -h, --help
          Print help (see a summary with '-h')

  -V, --version
          Print version
